Permissions: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent permissions and command policy. Permission maps
  capabilities to policy decisions (AUTO, APPROVAL, BLOCKED).

RiskLevels:
  R0:
    safe: Read file, list files, search
  R1:
    low: Create temp file, run formatter, run unit test
  R2:
    moderate: Modify source, install dependency, change config
  R3:
    high: DB migration, change security config, Docker infra change
  R4:
    critical: Production deployment, secret rotation, data migration
  R5:
    destructive: Delete production data, drop database, destroy infra

ApprovalMatrix:
  R0:
    AUTO
  R1:
    AUTO
  R2:
    AUTO / POLICY
  R3:
    APPROVAL
  R4:
    APPROVAL
  R5:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

CommandPolicy:
  go test:
    AUTO
  go build:
    AUTO
  docker build:
    AUTO
  docker push:
    APPROVAL
  git commit:
    AUTO
  git push:
    APPROVAL
  production deploy:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

EnvironmentPolicy:
  LOCAL:
    AUTO
  TEST:
    AUTO
  STAGING:
    APPROVAL
  PRODUCTION:
    EXPLICIT_APPROVAL

DatabasePolicy:
  SELECT:
    AUTO
  INSERT TEST DATA:
    AUTO
  UPDATE TEST:
    AUTO
  MIGRATION:
    APPROVAL
  DELETE:
    APPROVAL
  DROP:
    BLOCKED

SecretsPolicy:
  SECRET:
    NEVER_LOAD
  TOKEN:
    NEVER_LOAD
  PASSWORD:
    NEVER_LOAD
  PRIVATE_KEY:
    NEVER_LOAD
  API_KEY:
    NEVER_LOAD

PermissionRules:
  [PM1]  Permission = capability + policy + context.
  [PM2]  Project policy overrides global policy.
  [PM3]  Most specific policy wins (task > domain > project > global).
  [PM4]  When in conflict, safer policy wins.
  [PM5]  Secrets MUST NEVER be loaded into context.

State: +
  